+The opt-in planner microbenchmark exercises production construction and terminal
+skip registration:
+
+```powershell
+cargo bench --bench planner_skips --features bench-internals -- --case resume-4096 --iterations 100 --repeats 7
+cargo bench --bench planner_skips --features bench-internals -- --case new-unique --iterations 4096 --repeats 7
+```
+
+`resume-0` and `resume-4096` measure repeated `DumpPlanner` construction from an
+empty source and a prepared resume catalog, including `finish_profile` and
+destruction/join. `new-unique` and `new-duplicate` prepare one planner outside the
+timer, then register one prepared descriptor per iteration; queue extraction,
+`finish_profile`, and planner destruction are measured. Returned descriptors are
+verified byte-for-byte and in order after timing, then released outside timing.
+Fixture strings and directories are prepared outside every interval. Input
+descriptors are consumed inside the interval. `[planner-perf]` reports total
+input entries/path bytes, constructor/record counts, exact terminal/outgoing
+counts, a fixture fingerprint, and the same CPU and requested-allocation schema
+as the file benchmark. Use a separate `bench-allocations` build with
+`--allocations` for diagnostics; timing uses `bench-internals` without allocation
+instrumentation. Compare only matching cases, iterations, and instrumentation.
+
